DESCRIPTION:<b>WAITLIST</b>: <a href="https://duke.is/z/3y59" target="_bla
 nk">Click Here</a>\n\n<i>NOTE: We have reached the zoom room capacity for
  this event. Please complete the wait list survey\, and you will be sent 
 the meeting information if capacity opens up. </i>\n\nJoin us for the Duk
 e Office of Scientific Integrity's Research Town Hall "Using Generative A
 rtificial Intelligence in Research: Pairing innovation with integrity" on
  July 14th from 11:00am - 12:30pm.  \n\nGenerative artificial intelligenc
 e is changing the landscape of scientific integrity. Our expert panel of 
 speakers will share their perspectives on how AI can be responsibly integ
 rated into the research landscape without compromising integrity and rigo
 r.  The event will end with a panel discussion that will take questions p
 re-submitted through the registration link and submitted live during the 
 event. \n\nThis event is only open to current Duke faculty\, staff\, and 
 students. Attending this event fulfills the <b>RCR-200</b> requirement fo
 r Faculty and Staff and the <b>714</b> RCR credit for graduate students. 
 Participants must attend for at least 60 minutes to receive credit.
DURATION:PT1H30M
