CREATED:20260501T212128Z
DESCRIPTION:ADF Co-commissioned World Premiere\nProgram: Clair de Lune by 
 Jody Sperling\, New work by Pam Tanowitz\, ...Byzantium by Paul Taylor\, 
 Under the Rhythm by Robert Battle\nRunning time: 95 minutes\, includes tw
 o intermissions\nTickets: $40-$70\nTickets are purchased through Duke Uni
 versity's Box Office.\n\nPost-Performance Discussion on Wednesday\, July 
 15 at 7:30 pm.\n\nCompany Website: www.paultaylordance.org\n\nThis progra
 m includes four works by four choreographers. Clair de Lune by Jody Sperl
 ing is an homage to Loïe Fuller and mines her synaesthetic concept of col
 or harmony in which multi-hued lights are composed like musical notes int
 o luminous melodies and chords. Inspired by a poem and dedicated to his m
 other\, Under the Rhythm by Robert Battle\, the company's newly named and
  second Resident Choreographer\, is set to a jazzy\, energetic score feat
 uring Mahalia Jackson\, Ella Fitzgerald\, and Wycliffe Gordon. ...Byzanti
 um (1984) by Paul Taylor is a dark\, symbolic modern dance work that expl
 ores themes of religious tyranny\, power\, and human convolution\, inspir
 ed by Taylor's personal vision of the Byzantine era as a mix of intrigue 
 and ceremony. ADF alum and acclaimed choreographer Pam Tanowitz will crea
 te a new work for the company.\n\nPhoto Credit: Whitney Browne\n_________
 \n\nADF offers a 20% discount to Duke employees and $20 tickets to Duke s
 tudents (restrictions apply). To access your discount\, just log in with 
 your Duke Net ID at tickets.duke.edu.
DURATION:PT1H35M
