DESCRIPTION:ADF Co-commission\nProgram: MindScape\nRunning time: 60-70 min
 utes\, no intermission\nTickets: $30-$60\nTickets are purchased through D
 uke University's Box Office.\n\nPost-Performance Discussion on Saturday\,
  July 18 at 5 pm.\n\nCompany Website: www.shenweidancearts.org \n\nMindSc
 ape is the subject Shen Wei has been developing in his recent paintings a
 nd dances. This concept reflects Chinese culture\, permeating philosophy\
 , art\, and daily life. It is not merely a psychological state\, but a sp
 iritual pursuit and a way of life. Through self-cultivation\, continuous 
 exploration\, and elevation of one's "mindscape\," one pursues inner harm
 ony and transcendence. The work is being created in Guangzhou this Spring
  and will premiere in China in June before making its US premiere at ADF.
  The work will feature US dancers from Shen Wei Dance Arts and Chinese da
 ncers from Guangdong Modern Dance Company. This will be the first co-prod
 uction between the two dance companies.\n\nPhoto Credit: Filip Wolak\n___
 ______\n\nADF offers a 20% discount to Duke employees and $20 tickets to 
 Duke students (restrictions apply). To access your discount\, just log in
  with your Duke Net ID at tickets.duke.edu.
DURATION:PT1H
